hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27647","Haddathana Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Hisham, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me from Abu Salamah, from Ma'qil ibn Umm Ma'qil al-Asadi, he said: My mother wanted hajj, and her camel was emaciated, so she mentioned that to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: Perform umrah in Ramadan, for umrah in Ramadan is like hajj."
"27648","Haddathana Affan, he said: Haddathana Abu Awanah, he said: Haddathana Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, he said: The messenger of Marwan who was sent to Umm Ma'qil informed me, he said: She said: Abu Ma'qil came with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, as a pilgrim, then when Abu Ma'qil arrived, Umm Ma'qil said: You know that hajj is due upon me, and that you have a young camel, so give it to me that I may perform hajj upon it. He said: So he said to her: You know that I have made it in the path of Allah. She said: Then give me the harvest of your palm trees. He said: You know that it is the food of my family. She said: Then I shall speak to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and mention it to him. He said: So they both went walking until they entered upon him. He said: So she said to him: O Messenger of Allah, hajj is due upon me, and Abu Ma'qil has a young camel. Abu Ma'qil said: She spoke truly; I have made it in the path of Allah. He said: Give it to her that she may perform hajj upon it, for it is in the path of Allah. He said: Then when he gave her the young camel, she said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a woman who has grown old and sick, so is there a deed that suffices me for my hajj? He said: So he said: An umrah in Ramadan suffices for your hajj."
